          %h2#references References
          %p Accounts in the physics literature include:
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/0224"} doi:10.1142/0224
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CDF91-TOC.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CastellaniDAuriaFre-ChII7.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Accounts in the mathematical literature include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H.+Blaine+Lawson"}> H. Blaine Lawson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marie-Louise+Michelsohn"} Marie-Louise Michelsohn
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+geometry"} Spin geometry
            %li
              %p
                Anna Engels,
                %em Spin representations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/ag/ga/teaching/seminare/ws0304/repr.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian
            signature and with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT"} QFT
          %ul
            %li#Freed99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                %em
                  Lecture 3 of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Five+lectures+on+supersymmetry"} Five lectures on supersymmetry
                1999
            %li#Varadarajan04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veeravalli+Varadarajan"}> Veeravalli Varadarajan
                , section 7 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supersymmetry+for+mathematicians"}> Supersymmetry for mathematicians
                    \: An introduction
          %p
            With an eye towards application in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grand+unified+theory"} grand unified theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Howard+Georgi"}> Howard Georgi
              , §21 &amp; 22 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie Algebras In Particle Physics
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429499210"} doi:10.1201/9780429499210
          %p For the component notation traditionally used in physics see for instance
          %ul
            %li#vanProeyen99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"}> Antoine Van Proeyen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tools for supersymmetry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9910030"} arXiv:hep-th/9910030
            %li#Polchinski01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                , part II, appendix B of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+theory"} String theory
            %li#Brandt09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedemann+Brandt"}> Friedemann Brandt
                , section 2 of
                %em Supersymmetry algebra cohomology
                %em I: Definition and general structure
                J. Math. Phys.51:122302, 2010, (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2118"}> arXiv:0911.2118
                )
          %p
            For good math/physics discussion with special emphasis on the symplectic Majorana spinors and their role in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            see
          %ul
            %li#FigueroaOFarrill
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              ,
              %em Majorana spinors
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/Teaching/Lectures/Majorana.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Figueroa-MajoranaSpinors.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A clean summary of the relation of the real representation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+forms"} Hermitian forms
            over the real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            is in
